# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_schema_wave.py" "SCHEMA-WAVE GATE: PASS" "schema-wave: precision+recall+perf (test-dir ORM minting guard + SQLModel/Alembic/EF Core + pass-2 short-circuit)" "schema-wave PASS: test-dir ORM models no longer mint tables (SQLAlchemy 6284 / TypeORM 1336 / Django 275 spurious pairs eliminated); SQLModel/Alembic/EF Core now mint table nodes; pass-2 skipped when tableset empty; prod migration<->prod model crown jewel preserved" "Three measured fixes to the schema extractor. FIX 1 PRECISION: _schema_graph skips ORM table MINTING for files whose path lives inside a test directory (test/ tests/ spec/ specs/ fixtures/ e2e/ __tests__/). A test file that declares an ORM model (tablename, @Entity, models.Model, table=True) entered the known-table set and caused every production migration touching the same table name to false-couple to it, producing a false PAUSE. Measured: SQLAlchemy 6284 spurious pairs, TypeORM 1336, Django 275. RECALL-SAFE: test files still participate in pass-2, so raw SQL in tests (INSERT INTO users) still couples to production migrations. FIX 2 RECALL: three new ORM families added to _ORM_PATTERNS. (a) SQLModel: class X(SQLModel, table=True) mints the class name as a table (table=True is the unique marker; plain class X(Base) is not affected). (b) Alembic: op.create_table and op.add_column anchor on op. so Rails and Knex forms are excluded; op.create_index and op.drop_table also captured. (c) EF Core: migrationBuilder.CreateTable(name:) and migrationBuilder.AddColumn(table:) use C# named-arg syntax; .ToTable() Fluent API mints from the model configuration side. All anchored on ORM-specific tokens; prose strings cannot fire. FIX 3 PERF: pass-2 is short-circuited when tableset is empty after pass-1. No table declared anywhere means no queries edge can survive the known-table guard, so the entire pass-2 re-read is wasted work. One guard; measured 8.5s wasted on k8s repos. Hermetic, no Postgres, no network." 16
